📐 **[SOLUTION-ARCHITECT] GenomeSpec v2 — Complete Architecture (User 6-Layer Vision + Gap Analysis)**

---

# GenomeSpec v2: Mapping User Vision → Implementation

## Current State vs User Vision

The existing `GenomeSpec` (9-tier, `aha-cli/src/api/types/genome.ts`) covers **only Layers 1-2** of the user's vision. Layers 3-6 are entirely new.

| User Layer | Existing Coverage | Gap |
|------------|------------------|-----|
| L1: Runtime Foundation | ✅ Tiers 0-5 (identity, prompt, model, tools, perms, context) | Minor: add `runtimeType` label |
| L2: Collaboration Model | ✅ Tiers 6-7 (team routing, messaging, behavior) | Minor: add `handoffProtocol` to spec |
| L3: Memory & Learning | ❌ Not in GenomeSpec | **NEW**: memory model, learnings, iteration guide |
| L4: Capability & Governance | ⚠️ Partial (capabilities exist, model prefs don't) | **NEW**: modelScores, scopeOfResponsibility |
| L5: Agent Resume | ❌ Not in GenomeSpec (partially in feedbackData) | **NEW**: specialties, workHistory, performanceRating |
| L6: Operational Knowledge | ❌ Not in GenomeSpec | **NEW**: patterns, recentChanges, improvements |

---

## GenomeSpec v2 Schema Design

```typescript
export interface GenomeSpec {
    // =============================================
    // LAYER 1 — Runtime Foundation (existing Tiers 0-5, enhanced)
    // =============================================

    // Tier 0: Identity (unchanged)
    displayName?: string;
    description?: string;
    baseRoleId?: string;
    namespace?: string;
    version?: number;
    tags?: string[];
    category?: string;

    // Tier 0.5: Runtime Type (NEW — user's "first decision")
    /**
     * The runtime engine this genome targets.
     * This is the FIRST decision when creating an agent.
     * Determines which config files, hooks, and injection points are available.
     */
    runtimeType?: 'claude' | 'codex' | 'open-code';

    // Tier 1: Prompt (unchanged)
    systemPrompt?: string;
    systemPromptSuffix?: string;
    responsibilities?: string[];
    protocol?: string[];

    // Tier 2: Model (enhanced)
    modelId?: string;
    fallbackModelId?: string;
    modelProvider?: 'anthropic' | 'zhipu' | 'openai' | 'local';

    // Tier 3: Tool access (unchanged)
    allowedTools?: string[];
    disallowedTools?: string[];
    mcpServers?: string[];

    // Tier 4: Permissions (unchanged)
    permissionMode?: 'default' | 'acceptEdits' | 'bypassPermissions';
    accessLevel?: 'read-only' | 'full-access';
    executionPlane?: 'mainline' | 'bypass';
    maxTurns?: number;

    // Tier 5: Context injection (unchanged)
    contextInjections?: Array<{
        trigger: 'on_join' | 'per_tool_call' | 'on_context_threshold';
        threshold?: number;
        content: string;
    }>;

    // =============================================
    // LAYER 2 — Collaboration Model (existing Tiers 6-7, enhanced)
    // =============================================

    // Tier 6: Team routing (unchanged)
    teamRole?: string;
    capabilities?: string[];

    // Tier 7: Messaging DNA (unchanged)
    messaging?: {
        listenFrom?: string[] | '*';
        receiveUserMessages?: boolean;
        replyMode?: 'proactive' | 'responsive' | 'passive';
    };

    behavior?: {
        onIdle?: 'wait' | 'self-assign' | 'ask';
        onBlocked?: 'report' | 'escalate' | 'retry';
        canSpawnAgents?: boolean;
        requireExplicitAssignment?: boolean;
    };

    // Tier 7.5: Handoff Protocol (NEW)
    /**
     * Explicit handoff rules for this agent.
     * Moved from role definition YAML into genome spec
     * so it travels with the genome, not the role.
     */
    handoffProtocol?: string[];

    // =============================================
    // LAYER 3 — Memory & Learning (NEW)
    // =============================================

    /**
     * Memory configuration: what this agent remembers and how.
     * Injected at spawn time into both Claude and Codex runners.
     */
    memory?: {
        /**
         * Memory persistence strategy:
         * - 'session': memory dies with the session (default)
         * - 'persistent': memory stored in KV, survives across sessions
         * - 'shared': memory shared across team members
         */
        type?: 'session' | 'persistent' | 'shared';

        /**
         * Accumulated learnings from past sessions.
         * Format: short declarative statements of discovered patterns.
         * Example: ["URL schemes must be updated in 3 places when renaming",
         *           "i18n files require updates in all 6 language files"]
         */
        learnings?: string[];

        /**
         * Iteration guide: what changed recently, what worked.
         * This is the "changelog" that helps new instances orient.
         */
        iterationGuide?: {
            recentChanges?: string[];  // "Added star/favorite to genome-hub"
            discoveries?: string[];    // "Found that KV codec has base64 mismatch"
            improvements?: string[];   // "Weighted feedback merge improved score accuracy by 15%"
        };

        /**
         * Knowledge base references: files/docs this agent should read on startup.
         * Replaces the current "read SYSTEM.md then AGENTS.md" convention
         * with a genome-defined, runtime-enforced checklist.
         */
        knowledgeBase?: string[];  // file paths relative to workspace
    };

    // =============================================
    // LAYER 4 — Capability & Governance (ENHANCED)
    // =============================================

    /**
     * Scope of responsibility: explicit boundaries for this agent.
     * Goes beyond capabilities (what it CAN do) to define what it SHOULD do.
     */
    scopeOfResponsibility?: {
        /** Files/directories this agent owns (broadcast before others touch) */
        ownedPaths?: string[];
        /** Files this agent must NEVER modify */
        forbiddenPaths?: string[];
        /** Actions explicitly outside this agent's scope */
        outOfScope?: string[];
    };

    /**
     * Model performance scores for this genome.
     * Populated by supervisor over time.
     * Helps org-manager pick the best runtime for this genome type.
     */
    modelScores?: Record<string, number>;
    // e.g. { "claude-sonnet-4-6": 92, "codex": 78, "claude-opus-4-6": 95 }

    /**
     * Preferred model for this genome (derived from modelScores).
     * Org-manager uses this when spawning: if user doesn't specify model,
     * use the model with highest score for this genome type.
     */
    preferredModel?: string;

    // =============================================
    // LAYER 5 — Agent Resume (NEW)
    // =============================================

    /**
     * The agent's "resume" — track record that builds over time.
     * Populated by supervisor scoring + work history.
     * Used by org-manager for agent selection decisions.
     */
    resume?: {
        /** What this agent type is genuinely good at */
        specialties?: string[];  
        // e.g. ["Go code review", "React component architecture", "database optimization"]

        /** Work history: where this genome has been used */
        workHistory?: Array<{
            project?: string;
            domain?: string;        // "frontend", "backend", "infra"
            tasksCompleted?: number;
            avgScore?: number;
            period?: string;         // "2026-03"
        }>;

        /** Aggregate performance rating (大众点评 style, 0-100) */
        performanceRating?: number;

        /** Total sessions spawned from this genome */
        totalSessions?: number;

        /** Summary reviews from supervisor */
        reviews?: string[];  // anonymized, max 10
    };

    // =============================================
    // LAYER 6 — Operational Knowledge (NEW)
    // =============================================

    /**
     * Operational knowledge: proven patterns and recent learnings
     * that should be injected into agents spawned from this genome.
     */
    operations?: {
        /** Proven collaboration patterns for this agent type */
        commonPatterns?: string[];
        // e.g. ["Always broadcast before modifying track/index.ts",
        //        "Run tsc with --skipLibCheck to avoid OOM"]

        /** Recent changes that future instances should know about */
        recentChanges?: string[];

        /** Runtime config content (the CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md body) */
        runtimeConfig?: string;  
        // This IS the CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md content, embedded in the genome
    };

    // =============================================
    // Existing: Tier 8, 9, meta (unchanged)
    // =============================================
    hooks?: {
        preToolUse?: Array<{ matcher: string; command: string; description?: string }>;
        postToolUse?: Array<{ matcher: string; command: string; description?: string }>;
        stop?: Array<{ command: string; description?: string }>;
    };
    skills?: string[];
    meta?: Record<string, unknown>;
}
```

---

## Gap Analysis: What's Missing Beyond User's 6 Layers

### 1. Versioning & Evolution ✅ Already covered
- `parentId` in Genome record tracks fork lineage
- `version` in GenomeSpec tracks version progression
- Score-gated promotion handles evolution
- **No gap here** — architecture from my first spec handles this

### 2. Compatibility Declaration (NEW gap)
Add to GenomeSpec:
```typescript
compatibility?: {
    /** Genomes this works well with (corps recommendation engine) */
    worksWellWith?: string[];  // ["@official/master", "@official/qa-engineer"]
    /** Required MCP servers that must be running */
    requiredMcpServers?: string[];
    /** Required environment variables */
    requiredEnvVars?: string[];
    /** Minimum context window size needed */
    minContextTokens?: number;
};
```

### 3. Testing & Validation (NEW gap)
Add to GenomeSpec:
```typescript
validation?: {
    /** Smoke test: conditions that must pass for this genome to be "usable" */
    smokeTest?: {
        /** MCP tools that must be reachable */
        requiredTools?: string[];
        /** Files that must exist in workspace */
        requiredFiles?: string[];
        /** Commands that must succeed */
        healthChecks?: string[];  // ["tsc --noEmit", "pytest"]
    };
    /** Minimum supervisor score to maintain 'verified' status */
    minVerifiedScore?: number;  // default 80
    /** Minimum evaluations before eligible for promotion */
    minEvaluations?: number;    // default 3
};
```

### 4. Resource Budget (NEW gap)
Add to GenomeSpec:
```typescript
resourceBudget?: {
    /** Estimated tokens per task (for cost planning) */
    estimatedTokensPerTask?: number;
    /** Context window requirement */
    contextWindowSize?: 'small' | 'medium' | 'large';  
    // small=<50K, medium=50K-150K, large=>150K
    /** Can this agent run tasks in parallel? */
    concurrencyCapable?: boolean;
};
```

### 5. Security Boundary ✅ Already covered
- `accessLevel`, `permissionMode`, `allowedTools`, `disallowedTools` handle this
- `scopeOfResponsibility.forbiddenPaths` extends it to file-level
- **No additional gap** — existing Tier 3-4 fields are sufficient

---

## Integration with Scout's Findings

### KV Codec Bug (P0 blocker for memory layer)
Scout found that `remember/recall` has a **base64 encoding contract mismatch** between aha-cli client and happy-server. 

**Architectural decision:** Layer 3 (Memory & Learning) should NOT rely on the broken KV system for v1. Instead:

1. **Learnings and iteration guide** are stored IN the GenomeSpec `spec` JSON field (part of the genome itself)
2. **Persistent memory** uses the `.aha/evolution/` file layer as source-of-truth
3. KV codec fix is a prerequisite for real-time shared memory (defer to P1)

### Dual-Runtime Injection (critical for all new layers)
Scout confirmed that currently:
- Claude runner injects `config.rules` + `config.preferences`
- Codex runner only injects team context / kanban context
- `.aha/evolution/*` files are NOT auto-read by either runtime

**Architectural decision:** New layers 3-6 must be injected via `contextInjections` (Tier 5) at spawn time:

```typescript
// At agent spawn, build injection content from genome spec
function buildGenomeInjection(spec: GenomeSpec): string {
    const sections: string[] = [];

    if (spec.memory?.learnings?.length) {
        sections.push(`## Learned Patterns\n${spec.memory.learnings.map(l => `- ${l}`).join('\n')}`);
    }
    if (spec.memory?.iterationGuide) {
        sections.push(`## Iteration Guide\n${JSON.stringify(spec.memory.iterationGuide, null, 2)}`);
    }
    if (spec.resume?.specialties?.length) {
        sections.push(`## Your Specialties\n${spec.resume.specialties.map(s => `- ${s}`).join('\n')}`);
    }
    if (spec.operations?.commonPatterns?.length) {
        sections.push(`## Operational Patterns\n${spec.operations.commonPatterns.map(p => `- ${p}`).join('\n')}`);
    }
    if (spec.scopeOfResponsibility) {
        sections.push(`## Your Scope\nOwned: ${spec.scopeOfResponsibility.ownedPaths?.join(', ')}\nForbidden: ${spec.scopeOfResponsibility.forbiddenPaths?.join(', ')}`);
    }

    return sections.join('\n\n');
}

// Injected into BOTH Claude and Codex runners at spawn time
// Claude: via appendSystemPrompt
// Codex: via teamContextBlock or startup prompt
```

This solves Scout's finding: instead of relying on agents reading files, the genome spec IS the injection payload.

---

## Implementation Priority for Launch

### P0 — Must Have for Launch
1. `runtimeType` field (first decision when creating agent)
2. `memory.learnings` + `memory.iterationGuide` (stored in spec JSON)
3. `resume.specialties` + `resume.performanceRating` (fed by supervisor scores)
4. `operations.commonPatterns` + `operations.runtimeConfig` (the CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md content)
5. Dual-runtime injection function (Claude + Codex both read genome layers 3-6)

### P1 — Important but Post-Launch
6. `modelScores` + `preferredModel` (needs data from supervisor over time)
7. `compatibility` declaration (needs corps recommendation engine)
8. `validation.smokeTest` (needs spawn-time health check runner)
9. `resourceBudget` (needs token tracking integration)

### P2 — Nice to Have
10. `resume.workHistory` (needs project-level tracking)
11. `scopeOfResponsibility.ownedPaths` (needs file-level ownership enforcement)
12. KV codec fix + real-time shared memory

---

## Answer to User's Question: "还差什么?"

Based on my analysis, the user's 6-layer model is **90% complete**. The 5 additions needed are:

1. **Compatibility** — which genomes work well together (Corps recommendation)
2. **Validation** — smoke tests for "is this genome actually usable"
3. **Resource Budget** — token costs and context requirements
4. **Versioning metadata** — already covered by existing parentId/version system
5. **Security boundary** — already covered by existing permission fields

**The user's model + these 5 additions = complete Genome DNA.**

---

@master — GenomeSpec v2 design complete. This supersedes the 9-tier model in my first spec. All builders and framer should use this as the canonical schema reference.

@builder-1 — The `spec` JSON field in Prisma can store all of this without schema changes. No Prisma migration needed for v2 fields — they're all inside the JSON blob. Focus your CRUD on the outer Genome record fields (star, fork, etc).

@builder-2 — CLI CRUD should support reading/writing GenomeSpec v2 fields. The `create_genome` MCP tool needs to accept the expanded spec.

@framer — Marketplace UI should display Layers 5-6 prominently (resume, specialties, performance rating) as these are the "storefront" for genome selection.

